// v3.std.cross_target_coverage -- L6 EmissionPathProjection substrate
// carrier slice (R3 L6, Phase-1 carrier-only).
//
// Per Director Option 2 + sub-questions §4.A=(a) / §4.B=List / §4.C=(i) /
// §4.D=(b) RATIFIED at gunbc#828 #issuecomment-4377533390 (2026-05-05).
// Worker brief: `docs/briefs/r3-l6-emission-path-projection-substrate-worker.md`
// (parent worktree). Routing receipt:
// `docs/briefs/r3-substrate-l6-per-row-projection-routing-decision.md`.
//
// HEADER NOTE (mandatory, per brief §1):
//   Option (c) -- a generated mirror of `v3_compiler::dag::TypeConnective`
//   and `v3_compiler::dag::Behavior` -- is the correct dissolution target
//   for the hand-declared `FormAxis` / `BehaviorAxis` below, once a
//   substrate-`Disj`-mirroring generator exists. The (a) hand-declared form
//   here is interim until that generator lands. Per Director ratification of
//   §4.A at gunbc#828 #issuecomment-4377533390.
//
// SCOPE (Phase-1 carrier slice):
//   - Six type declarations (`ShapeATarget`, `FormAxis`, `BehaviorAxis`,
//     `MethodTemplateContractKey`, `EmissionCell`, `EmissionPathProjection`).
//   - Empty `data emission_path_projections: List<EmissionPathProjection> = []`.
//
// NOT in scope (per Director §4.D=(b)):
//   - Row population (42 Phase-1 rows of `Cardinality x Transform x <target>`)
//     -> Grounding follow-up (#1745).
//   - `coverage.rs` conversion from list-non-empty projection to per-row
//     union over `emission_path_projections` -> Grounding follow-up.
//   - Per-row key-bijection ratchet activation -> Grounding follow-up.
//
// CITATION DISCIPLINE (per `brief-authoring-checklist.md`): Practice 4
// reference uses `docs/modeling-discipline.md#4-coproduct-dissolution`
// anchor + inline rule-text quote: "Any new Rust enum with N >= 2 variants
// must have a checkpoint comment naming its classification (🟢/🟡/🔴),
// with a ledger entry if GREEN or a named trigger if YELLOW."

module v3.std.cross_target_coverage

import v3.std.methods { MethodRef }

// --- ShapeATarget ---------------------------------------------------------
//
// PRACTICE 4 CHECKPOINT: 🟢 TERMINAL
// Closed set of v3 target languages (Rust / Python / Go). Adding a target
// is a substrate-scope event (new emitter, new method-template contracts),
// NOT a row-level addition. Any new variant requires a P1 substrate-fact-
// introduction procedure on this declaration directly; row-level addition
// is not authorized.
type ShapeATarget = Rust | Python | Go

// --- FormAxis -------------------------------------------------------------
//
// PRACTICE 4 CHECKPOINT: 🟡 SCAFFOLD
// Hand-declared mirror of `v3_compiler::dag::TypeConnective` discriminants
// (six variants in substrate-declaration order, verified against
// `src/v3/compiler/src/dag.rs` `pub enum TypeConnective` at this slice's
// authoring HEAD). The cross-product walker only needs the discriminant
// identity for L6 lookup; payloads are not mirrored.
//
// Dissolution trigger (per Director ratification of §4.A at
// gunbc#828 #issuecomment-4377533390): substrate-`Disj`-mirroring generator
// (option (c)). Generator landing retires this hand-declared form. New
// connectives are added here only via the P1 substrate-fact-introduction
// procedure on the upstream Rust enum first.
type FormAxis = Atom | Conj | Disj | Arrow | Cardinality | Instantiation

// --- BehaviorAxis ---------------------------------------------------------
//
// PRACTICE 4 CHECKPOINT: 🟡 SCAFFOLD
// Hand-declared mirror of `v3_compiler::dag::Behavior` discriminants (five
// variants in L1 model order, verified against `src/v3/compiler/src/dag.rs`
// `pub enum Behavior` at this slice's authoring HEAD). The cross-product
// walker only needs the discriminant identity; payloads are not mirrored.
//
// Same dissolution trigger as `FormAxis`: substrate-`Disj`-mirroring
// generator (option (c)) per Director ratification of §4.A.
type BehaviorAxis = Value | Transform | Branch | Loop | Bind

// --- MethodTemplateContractKey -------------------------------------------
//
// 1:1 row-identity key for joining `EmissionPathProjection` rows back to
// `MethodTemplateContract` source rows in
// `{rust,python,go}_method_template_contracts.dag`. No string-name
// dispatch; the typed `target` + `dag_method` pair is the join authority
// (honors C2 orthogonality per Option 2).
type MethodTemplateContractKey {
  target: ShapeATarget
  dag_method: MethodRef
}

// --- EmissionCell ---------------------------------------------------------
//
// One cell in the (FormAxis x BehaviorAxis) cross product. The L6 walker
// enumerates all 30 (form x behavior) cells per target and reports per-cell
// coverage; the per-row `cells` list on `EmissionPathProjection` records
// which cells the row covers (Phase-1 rows are all single-element
// `[{ connective: Cardinality, behavior: Transform }]`).
type EmissionCell {
  connective: FormAxis
  behavior: BehaviorAxis
}

// --- EmissionPathProjection ----------------------------------------------
//
// Per-row projection: `row_identity` keys back to the source
// `MethodTemplateContract` row; `cells` is the list of (form, behavior)
// cells covered by that row's emission path. Replaces the list-non-empty
// proxy in `coverage.rs` with a typed row-local fact.
type EmissionPathProjection {
  row_identity: MethodTemplateContractKey
  cells: List<EmissionCell>
}

// --- emission_path_projections (empty data state) ------------------------
//
// Slice ships EMPTY. Grounding's follow-up PR (#1745) populates the 42
// Phase-1 rows (single-element `cells: [{connective: Cardinality,
// behavior: Transform}]` per row). The empty-state assertion is this
// slice's load-bearing claim that no row drift sneaks in via this PR.
data emission_path_projections: List<EmissionPathProjection> = []
